        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r8d" value="publish it" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b3b3b3;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="v1">
          <mxGeometry x="445" y="584" width="240" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="retry" value="&lt;b&gt;Retry policy&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;transient · infra · timeout retry with backoff until max_attempts, then become&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;dead&lt;/b&gt;. &lt;b&gt;data&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;code&lt;/b&gt; are terminal immediately — retrying a deterministic parse failure three&lt;br&gt;times only produces three identical stack traces. So the data/code split is for TRIAGE, not control&lt;br&gt;flow: it is what tells &quot;400 sessions our parser cannot handle&quot; from &quot;the last release is broken&quot;.&lt;/font&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="v1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="675" width="660" height="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gap" value="&lt;b&gt;Both halves are pinned&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;The chain on the right pins the PROCESSOR. The &lt;b&gt;worker&lt;/b&gt; is pinned&lt;br&gt;separately, because nothing can discover the image it was started&lt;br&gt;from — it has to be told:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;compose: image: ${VRF_IMAGE:?} &amp;#160;(refuses to start unpinned)&lt;br&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;compose: VRF_WORKER_IMAGE_URI=${VRF_IMAGE:?}&lt;br&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#8594; Worker.worker_image() &amp;#8594; heartbeat &amp;#8594; workers.worker_image&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A distinct variable from the children's PROCESSOR_IMAGE_URI: the two hold&lt;br&gt;the same value today (one image, three entrypoints), and sharing the name&lt;br&gt;would bake that in and make each layer unattributable to itself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;doctor&lt;/b&gt; refuses a campaign whose worker cannot say what it is, unless&lt;br&gt;processor.allow_unpinned &amp;#8212; which relaxes BOTH halves, since a run&lt;br&gt;allowed to be unreproducible is allowed to be so on both sides.&lt;/font&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="v1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="790" width="540" height="215" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
